{title: Brother To Brother}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{tempo: 136}

Lyrics
[C](Short introduction)

Verse 1
Thank you, my brother,
[G]for [A7]being [F]around,
For [C]stopping to listen
[B]when [A]I was cast down.
[E]For [F]being a [Fm]brother
[F]and [Am]lending [A]a [A#]hand,
For [C]prayers that you offered
that helped [F]me to [G#]stand.

Refrain
Brother [C]to [B]brother
[Bm]is [A]how we [C#]must [F]live
There are [C]times we receive,
[G]just as times [Am7]we're to give.
[C]The [F]care and compassion
are [Am]stars [Am7]in [C]your [A#]crown
[C7]For [C]being my [D]brother
[F]when I [C]was cast down.

Verse 2
[Am7]So [C]take heart, my brother
[G]if [Am7]ever you're down.
[F]I'll stand [C]right beside [Bm]you
and [Am7]always be found.
[C]And [F]when we've departed,
though time [Am]is like sand,
[A#]We'll rejoice [C]up in heaven,
[Dm7]as brother [F]and [G#]friend.
[C](Repeat Refrain)
[C]Brother to [Em7]brother
[G]is [Em]how [Am]we must [F]live
There are times [C]we receive,
[G]just as [Am]times we're to [C]give.
The care [F]and compassion
[Fm]are stars [Am]in your [A#]crown
For [C]being my [Dm7]brother
[F]when I [G]was cast [C]down.
